invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify_point.c
catches: p256_verify_equiv_test
reason: the host verifier's mixed addition, which adds an entry of the
  table of multiples of G, gives the point at infinity when the running
  sum is that entry, where the sum is its double. The case of
  bin/p256_verify_equiv_test under the key G/2 with u1 = 1 and u2 = 2
  brings the running sum to G just before G is added, and wants the
  signature taken.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_sub(&rr, &s2, &a->y);
    if (fe_is_zero(&h)) {
        if (fe_is_zero(&rr)) {
            point_double(o, a);
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_sub(&rr, &s2, &a->y);
    if (fe_is_zero(&h)) {
        if (fe_is_zero(&rr)) {
            memset(o, 0, sizeof *o);
